force-path-style: litestream 0.5.17 has no such replica option. It was
  accepted as a replica URL query parameter in the 2026-09-28 file
  rehearsal with no error and no observable effect, so it is recorded as
  NOT SUPPORTED rather than tested. Addressing is decided by the URL host:
  a bucket in the path is path-style, a bucket in the host is virtual-host.
THE SCHEME IN endpoint= IS MANDATORY, and getting it wrong is silent.
  Measured here: endpoint=https://<host>:<port> works; endpoint=<host>:<port>
  with no scheme makes 0.5.17 speak PLAINTEXT http, so against an https
  endpoint the request is rejected as a TLS error before the signature is
  checked: 0 objects written, no rejected request, and nothing in
  litestream's log naming the cause. Every SigV4-signed request in that
  mode would also have carried the request signature in cleartext.
skip-verify (TLS): NOT USED, and the packet now proves why it does not
  need to be. 0.5.17 has a skip-verify replica option, and a rehearsal
  could use it to accept the self-signed endpoint. It is deliberately
  not used: the "untrusted-ca" variant above runs the SAME working URL
  with the rehearsal CA removed, and a gate that only passes because
  verification was switched off would then show up as a failure.
  AWS_CA_BUNDLE is the documented AWS way to add a CA and 0.5.17 ABORTS
  on it: "cannot load aws config: unable to add custom RootCAs
  HTTPClient, has no WithTransportOptions". SSL_CERT_FILE is read by
  Go instead and works. Trust in this run: SSL_CERT_FILE=/tmp/dg-sandbox-run-X8UpUx/endpoint/tls/bundle.pem (system roots + the rehearsal endpoint's self-signed CA); verification stays ON, and AWS_CA_BUNDLE is deliberately NOT set because litestream 0.5.17 aborts on it

minimal working replica URL (against the configured endpoint):
  s3://dg-sandbox-rehearsal/gate3?endpoint=https://127.0.0.1:53281&region=us-east-1
  i.e. the endpoint parameter carries the scheme. Without it, this URL
  replicates nothing and says nothing about why.

NOTE: `replica.path` cannot carry a URL. `path: s3://...` fails with
  "replica path cannot be a url, please use the url field instead".

