Why the ORDER matters: the owner credential and the scoped key are stored
as HASHES in metadata.sqlite, and a restored file is only useful if the
gateway accepts that file as its registry. Starting a second gateway on
the recovered directory, with a key minted before the loss, is the only
observation that distinguishes "the file came back" from "the
authorization context came back".

